# playpick: mode=raid boss=flasks spec=warlock:destruction size=10
# difficulty=normal view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# First use of the `ladder` command in this job's history. docs/playtest.md's
# own worked example (The Bonegrinder, 10 players, normal, four pulls under
# `learn`) has sat in the spec since the job was seeded and no committed
# script has ever actually called it -- checked by grepping all 188 prior
# .play files for the literal command before writing this one. The Two
# Flasks already has an idle/good pair on this exact cell (-20.play and
# 2026-09-25-20.play: idle takenPerMin=1314.4, good takenPerMin=1678.0,
# direction.md #1), so a ladder curve here lands next to real numbers to
# discriminate against, the way the spec's own Bonegrinder table does.
# Four pulls, not nine -- docs/playtest.md says ask for fewer seconds when
# nine would cost too long a foreground block; four pulls at up to 90s each
# is enough to see whether any curve appears at all.
open #b=flasks&s=10&h=0
targets
tap class:warlock:destruction
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot ladder-start

ladder 4 90
bill
says
state
shot ladder-end
